{"paper": "SSC-CPO-Tier1-27-Jun-2024-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 50, "tagged_count": 50, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Two similar triangles of ΔXYZ and ΔLMN. If area of (ΔXYZ) = 16 cm2, area of (ΔLMN) = 25 cm2 and YZ = 2.4 cm, then the measure of MN is:", "options": [{"text": "3 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "1 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "4 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "2 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "A train covers a distance of 56 km in 35 minutes. Travelling at the same speed, in how many seconds will the train cover a distance of 720 metres?", "options": [{"text": "32", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "24", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "Simplify", "options": [{"text": "574", "added": false}, {"text": "546", "added": false}, {"text": "561", "added": false}, {"text": "526", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "Study the given table and answer the question that follows. The table shows the number of students in various courses in various cities A, B, C, D and E in India during the academic year 2022-2023. What was the average number of students in Science course in the all the cities altogether during the academic year 2022-2023?", "options": [{"text": "2220", "added": false}, {"text": "2200", "added": false}, {"text": "2250", "added": false}, {"text": "2240", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "A man travels some distance at a speed of 12 km/h and returns at a speed of 8 km/h. If the total time taken by him is 3 hours and 45 minutes, then the total distance (in km) travelled is:", "options": [{"text": "42", "added": false}, {"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "32", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "A rectangular sheet of metal is 60 cm by 25 cm. Equal squares of side 5 cm are cut off at the corners and the remainder is folded up to form an open rectangular box. Find the volume of the box.", "options": [{"text": "3750 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "5750 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "4750 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "2750 cm3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "frustum-prism-pyramid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "150%", "added": false}, {"text": "130%", "added": false}, {"text": "100%", "added": false}, {"text": "120%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "Simplify 35 - [30 + {10 + (12 - 10 - 4)}].", "options": [{"text": "−3", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "−2", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "A grocer purchased 10 kg rice for ₹700. He spends some amount on transportation and then sells it for ₹1,400. If the percentage of profit made by the grocer is 30%, then what is the amount (in₹)he spends on transportation? (Round off to the nearest integer)", "options": [{"text": "300", "added": false}, {"text": "380", "added": false}, {"text": "377", "added": false}, {"text": "350", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "If two circles of radii 35 cm and 25 cm touch each other externally, then the length (in cm) of a common tangent is (Rounded off to 2 decimal places)", "options": [{"text": "60.00", "added": false}, {"text": "59.16", "added": false}, {"text": "45.29", "added": false}, {"text": "52.25", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "A man’s speed in still water is 4 km/h more than the speed of the current. If the man takes a total of 10 h to cover 45 km downstream and 35 km upstream, then the speed of the man in still water is:", "options": [{"text": "15 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "22 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "18 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "20 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Boats-Streams", "sub": "still-water-and-stream-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "In a store, an item with marked price of ₹82,500 is available at a discounted price of ₹79,200. What is the percentage of discount given on that item?", "options": [{"text": "1%", "added": false}, {"text": "4%", "added": false}, {"text": "2%", "added": false}, {"text": "3%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "If 24 people can build 90 identical walls in 25 days, then how many more days will 27 people require to build 162 such walls?", "options": [{"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "group-work", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1731", "added": false}, {"text": "2856", "added": false}, {"text": "1724", "added": false}, {"text": "2464", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "700", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "350", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "The population of a town increases 8% annually. If its present population is 1,42,560, what was the population one year ago?", "options": [{"text": "1,33,000", "added": false}, {"text": "1,34,000", "added": false}, {"text": "1,31,000", "added": false}, {"text": "1,32,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "population-and-depreciation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "20%", "added": false}, {"text": "25%", "added": false}, {"text": "28%", "added": false}, {"text": "22.5%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "−10", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "−15", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "In a ∆ABC, angle BAC = 30° and angle BCA = 60°. If AC = 13 cm and AB = 12 cm, then BC is equal to:", "options": [{"text": "7 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "5 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "4 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "6 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "18 workers can complete a piece of work in 96 days. They start working together and after 26 days 10 more workers join them. In how many days in all will the work be completed?", "options": [{"text": "72", "added": false}, {"text": "69", "added": false}, {"text": "71", "added": false}, {"text": "70", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 26, "text": "Study the given table and answer the question that follows. The table shows the number of students in various courses in various cities A, B, C, D and E in India during the academic year 2022-2023. In all the cities altogether, what is the difference between the students of science and those of MBA?", "options": [{"text": "4240", "added": false}, {"text": "4440", "added": false}, {"text": "4540", "added": false}, {"text": "4340", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 27, "text": "A person deposited some amount of money in the bank at simple interest. After 20 years, the amount became nine times the amount deposited. In how many years will the amount become 13 times the amount if the interest rate remains the same?", "options": [{"text": "28", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "23", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 28, "text": "In alloys A and B, the ratio of lead to tin is 5 : 3 and 3 : 1, respectively. 80 kg of alloy A and 100 kg of alloy B are mixed together to form a new alloy. What is the amount of tin (in kg) in the new alloy?", "options": [{"text": "90", "added": false}, {"text": "55", "added": false}, {"text": "81.3", "added": false}, {"text": "68", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mixture-Alligation", "sub": "mixture-price", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 29, "text": "In an election between two candidates, 10% of the voters did not cast their votes and 75 votes were found invalid. The winner got 50% of the total votes expected and won by 170 votes. How many voters were enrolled in the voters’ list?", "options": [{"text": "800", "added": false}, {"text": "850", "added": false}, {"text": "950", "added": false}, {"text": "855", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 30, "text": "If the radius of a sphere is increased by 40%, then find the percentage increase in its surface area.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 31, "text": "The value of (42)2 + 4 × 4 ÷ 4 − 4 is:", "options": [{"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "42", "added": false}, {"text": "43", "added": false}, {"text": "44", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 32, "text": "A product was offered at a 10% trade discount on the marked price. After a cash discount of 10%, the product was sold for ₹7,290. The marked price (in ₹) is:", "options": [{"text": "8,510", "added": false}, {"text": "9,000", "added": false}, {"text": "8,900", "added": false}, {"text": "8,720", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 33, "text": "R reaches office from home in 30 minutes and comes back in 20 minutes. The distance to his office from home is 12.5 km. What is his average speed (in km/h) from home to office and then back home?", "options": [{"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "60", "added": false}, {"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 34, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 35, "text": "A dishonest dealer sells his goods at 20% loss on the cost price but uses a faulty weight that weighs 25% less. His profit or loss percentage (rounded off to 2 decimal places) is:", "options": [{"text": "6.67%, profit", "added": false}, {"text": "3.33%, profit", "added": false}, {"text": "3.33%, loss", "added": false}, {"text": "6.67%, loss", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "dishonest-dealer", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 36, "text": "Which of the following is true when x = SinA + CosA; y = SecA + CosecA?", "options": [{"text": "y + 2x = x2 y", "added": false}, {"text": "y(1 + x2 ) = 2x", "added": false}, {"text": "y(1 - 2x2 ) = x", "added": false}, {"text": "y - 2x = x2 y", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 37, "text": "In an election, A received 27% of the votes and B received 125,982 votes. 19% did not cast their votes. Find the number of votes received by A.", "options": [{"text": "1,88,973", "added": false}, {"text": "62,991", "added": false}, {"text": "57,827", "added": false}, {"text": "44,327", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 38, "text": "Simplify [{38 - ( - 6)} × {9 - (8 - 1)}] ÷ [4 × {6 + ( - 4)}].", "options": [{"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "22", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 39, "text": "Mitu can do a piece of work in 12 hours, Titu and Situ together in 2 hours, and Mitu and Situ together in 3 hours. How long will Titu alone take to do it?", "options": [{"text": "6 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "4 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "7 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "8 hours", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 40, "text": "Triangle DEF is an equilateral triangle with a side length of 12 cm. If point G is the mid- point of side DE, what is the length (in cm) of side FG?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "lines-and-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 41, "text": "The ratio of marks of A and B is 3 : 4 and the ratio of marks of B and C is 4 : 5. If the difference in the marks of C and A is 30, then how much marks does B get?", "options": [{"text": "52", "added": false}, {"text": "60", "added": false}, {"text": "56", "added": false}, {"text": "64", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 42, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "i